## Step 4: Why does this work?

- The heap holds only the largest `k` numbers encountered so far.
- Whenever it contains more than `k` numbers, we remove the smallest.
- At the end, the smallest number among the largest `k` numbers is the kth largest overall.

Time complexity: \\(O(n\log k)\\). Space complexity: \\(O(k)\\).

